# React (Renderer)

React 19 function components only. The renderer reaches the main process solely
through `window.electronApi`.

## Components

- Function components; name the props interface `<Component>Props`.
- Compose class names with `clsx`; group related Tailwind (v4) classes across
  lines for readability.
- Use `lucide-react` for icons and the shared primitives in `@/ui` (`Button`,
  `Modal`, `Switch`, …) instead of re-building them.

## Hooks & effects

- Stabilize values passed into deps or down to children with `useCallback` /
  `useMemo`.
- Guard async effect work with an `isMounted` flag and clean up listeners /
  subscriptions on unmount (unsubscribe functions returned by `electronApi`).
- Track superseded async work (e.g. rapid model reloads) with a request-id `ref`
  so a stale in-flight result can't clobber newer state (see `ModelContext`).

## Context

- Providers memoize their value object and expose a `use<Name>` hook.
- The hook throws a clear error when used outside its provider
  (`useModel must be used within a ModelProvider`), unless a documented
  fallback is intentional (see `LocaleContext`, used by leaf components in tests).
- Create context with `createContext<T | null>(null)` and read it with `use()`.

## User-facing text & i18n

- Never hard-code display strings. Use `const { t } = useTranslation()` and a
  message key; interpolate with `t(key, params)`.
- Surface recoverable errors through `useAlert().showAlert(t('...'), 'error')`
  rather than throwing to the user.
